From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:58:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc: AiMesh channel fit - a node needs the whole channel, flag
 4 is DFS, unknown DFS counts as DFS

Owner (RT-AX92U node, v3.4.6): the node's 5 GHz backhaul stayed off. The node
drops 116-128 on its 30-minute radar lock-out and, being 160 MHz, cannot hold
100/160 then; the fit rated 100/160 usable under the 80 MHz cap and read the
router's own cleared DFS block as non-DFS. A node that does the width needs
the whole channel; flag 4 in the controller's list is DFS; a channel a node
stops listing is held for 6 h. Owner-confirmed on the _r4 test build (37 fits,
100/160 excluded, the backhaul up on 149/80).

Region-neutral follow-up: when the router's own entry is missing from the mesh
channel lists, an undetermined DFS status now counts as DFS, so the fit can
neither re-allow nor move onto a DFS channel on a guess; it holds and says why
(reaper_bwfloor.c wording).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
